gs.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"topic-section\">\n    <details>\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Preceded By</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">1</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Preceded By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/lord-of-the-rings/books/the-hobbit\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            The Hobbit\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>The Hobbit precedes the War of the Ring.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"topic-section\">\n    <details>\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Adaptation Of</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">1</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Adaptation Of\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/lord-of-the-rings/peter-jackson\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Peter Jackson\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Jackson adapted LOTR into films.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"did-you-know\">\n    <h2>Did you know?</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>The Lord of the Rings is also referenced as LOTR, Lord of the Rings, Middle-earth.</li><li>The saga turns on the One Ring.</li><li>Tolkien wrote The Lord of the Rings.</li><li>Frodo is the story&#039;s Ring-bearer.</li><li>The War of the Ring is the saga&#039;s climax.</li><li>Evidence around The Lord of the Rings is classified as fiction on Ton-o-Lore.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is The Lord of the Rings?</h2>\n    <p>\n        <strong>The Lord of the Rings</strong> is\n        <a href=\"/lord-of-the-rings/jrr-tolkien\" class=\"entity-link\">J.R.R. Tolkien</a>'s epic of\n        <a href=\"/lord-of-the-rings/shire/frodo-baggins\" class=\"entity-link\">Frodo Baggins</a>,\n        the\n        <a href=\"/lord-of-the-rings/fellowship-of-the-ring\" class=\"entity-link\">Fellowship</a>, and the quest to destroy\n        <a href=\"/lord-of-the-rings/one-ring\" class=\"entity-link\">the One Ring</a>\n        forged by\n        <a href=\"/lord-of-the-rings/mordor/sauron\" class=\"entity-link\">Sauron</a>\n        in\n        <a href=\"/lord-of-the-rings/mordor\" class=\"entity-link\">Mordor</a>.\n    </p>\n</section>","word_count":1332,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"a980f59b-8fd7-4c17-a3c6-1e1f0ab92955","name":"The Lord of the Rings","slug":"lord-of-the-rings","type":"work","kind":"work","type_label":"Work","short_description":"The Lord of the Rings is an epic high fantasy novel written by J.R.R. Tolkien, which was later fitted as a trilogy. The story began as a sequel to Tolkien's earlier fantasy book , and soon developed into a much larger…","description":"The Lord of the Rings is an epic high fantasy novel written by J.R.R. Tolkien, which was later fitted as a trilogy. The story began as a sequel to Tolkien's earlier fantasy book , and soon developed into a much larger story. At publication, it was divided into (1954), (1955), and (1955). Around 1968, one-volume editions started to be published in both hardcover and paperback, but both those editions are now exceedingly rare.\n\nWritten in stages between 1937 and 1949, with much of it during World War II, it was originally published in three volumes in 1954 and 1955. It has since been reprinted numerous times and translated into at least 38 different languages, becoming one of the most popular works of twentieth-century literature.\n\nThe action in The Lord of the Rings is set in what the author conceived to be the lands of the real Earth, inhabited by humanity but placed in a fictional past, before familiar history but after the fall of his version of Atlantis, Númenor. Tolkien gave this setting a modern English name, Middle-earth, a rendering of the Old English Middangeard.\n\nThe story concerns peoples such as Hobbits, Elves, Men, Dwarves, Wizards, and Orcs (called goblins in The Hobbit), and centers on the Ring of Power made by the Dark Lord Sauron. Starting from quiet beginnings in the Shire, the story ranges across Middle-earth and follows the courses of the War of the Ring. The main story is followed by six appendices that provide a wealth of historical and linguistic background material, as well as an index listing every character, place, song, and sword.","evidence":"fiction","universe":"lord-of-the-rings","aliases":["LOTR","Lord of the Rings","Middle-earth"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/lotr/images/1/11/The_Lord_of_the_Rings_First_Copies.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/360?cb=20130619012726","image_source":"https://lotr.fandom.com/wiki/The_Lord_of_the_Rings","image_credit":"Fair-use identification thumbnail via Fandom. Character / franchise art © Tolkien Estate / New Line / Warner Bros. / Amazon (as applicable). Not free or redistributable artwork.","image_license":"fair_use","image_usage":"fair_use_identification","image_alt":"Identification thumbnail for The Lord of the Rings"},"connections":[],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"lord-of-the-rings","title":"The Lord of the Rings is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"The Lord of the Rings, The Hobbit, Middle-earth, and all related names and characters are trademarks of Middle-earth Enterprises, the Tolkien Estate, and/or their respective rights holders. Ton-o-Lore is an independent, unofficial fan and informational project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those rights holders. Identification logos and thumbnails, when shown, are low-resolution images used under a fair-use rationale for commentary and identification only — not free or redistributable artwork."},"subject":{"id":"lord-of-the-rings","name":"The Lord of the Rings","theme":"lord-of-the-rings","path":"/lord-of-the-rings","logo":{"license":"fair_use","usage":"fair_use_identification","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/The_Lord_of_the_Rings_logo.svg/330px-The_Lord_of_the_Rings_logo.svg.png","alt":"The Lord of the Rings logo","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Lord_of_the_Rings_logo.svg","credit":"Fair-use identification logo via Wikimedia Commons. © Middle-earth Enterprises / Tolkien Estate / respective rights holders."},"categories":["books","movies"]}}